<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<speak version="1.1" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis" xml:lang="en-GB">
<!-- The Watch Below, Chapter 76: Seven. Point of view: Calder. -->
<p><s>Chapter Seventy-six.</s></p><break time="800ms"/>
<p><s>Seven.</s></p><break time="1800ms"/>
<!-- p1 · tension: counting down, calm · Corvin -->
<p><prosody rate="97%">“Six,” said Corvin, as the flame touched the next notch.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p2 · tension -->
<p><prosody rate="97%">The dust came down out of the dome in a thin grey stream onto the carved stone between them. Small stones with it, pattering. Over their heads, through the rock, through the floor of the tower, the sound of <sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub> digging. Claws in stone. Closer. A second crack ran across the dome from the passage to the far wall.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p3 -->
<p>The men holding <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub> looked up.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p4 · Corvin -->
<p>“Five.”</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p5 -->
<p>Below the ledge, out in the dark, the six chains groaned.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p6 · dread -->
<p><prosody rate="96%">All of them at once. Going taut, the way they’d gone taut before, but further. Harder. A sound so deep it wasn’t a sound, it was the rock round them shaking, and it didn’t stop. It held. And held. Like a rope with a horse leaning back on it, a horse the size of a hill.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p7 -->
<p>The candle-flame on the floor beside the iron boss bent sideways and stood up again.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p8 -->
<p>The letters in the stone disc were brighter. <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub> saw it under his own knees. The rings of them coming up white out of the grey, ring after ring, like coals coming up when you work the bellows, and not going down again.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p9 -->
<p>On the edge of the disc the grey man got to his feet.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p10 · Corvin -->
<p>“Four,” said Corvin.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p11 · tension -->
<p><prosody rate="97%">He hadn’t moved. He knelt on the iron boss in the middle of the stone disc with his long pale hand on the bow of the key and his eyes on the candle, calm, as a man kneels at a wayside shrine. He didn’t look up at the dome, or the dust, or <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub>.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p12 · urgent · Calder (bond, to Kharrak); Calder (bond, to Kharrak), urgent -->
<p><prosody rate="105%"><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB"><sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub>,</prosody> said <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub>. <prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB"><sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub>, now, now, now…</prosody></prosody></p>
<break time="1600ms"/><!-- scene break -->
<!-- p13 · Corvin -->
<p>“Three.”</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p14 -->
<p>The dome came in.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p15 · action -->
<p><prosody rate="104%">The part over the passage, where the crack was. It came down in one great slab, rock and earth and stone, and the noise of it was louder than the river going out, and through the hole where it had been, out of the dark and the dust, came <sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub>.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p16 · action -->
<p><prosody rate="104%">Head first. Rust-red, filthy, bleeding from a long cut down his side, with his claws still out from the digging and the fire coming up in his throat. He came through the hole in the dome into the chamber with the floor of the tower coming down round him in pieces, and the light of his fire went over everything, white, and the men holding <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub> let go.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p17 -->
<p>They didn’t decide to. They saw a dragon come through the roof and their hands opened.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p18 -->
<p>The grey man didn’t run. He planted his feet on the white letters and threw his hands up at <sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub>’s head.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p19 -->
<p>The weight hit <sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub> in the face. <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub> felt it through the red mark, like a fist on his own nose. <sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub>’s head went back and sideways and the fire in his throat went up into the broken dome instead of out, and he came down off the rubble onto his knees on the edge of the disc, shaking his head.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p20 · dread -->
<p><prosody rate="96%">The grey man fell over. Straight down, like a coat dropped off a peg. <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub> saw his face as he went, and his hair, and his hair had gone white from the roots, all of it, in a breath.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p21 -->
<p><sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub> went for the key.</p>
<break time="1600ms"/><!-- scene break -->
<!-- p22 -->
<p>He was a pace from it. He’d been a pace from it the whole time, with four men holding him. He went across the pace on his knees and got his hand on Corvin’s wrist.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p23 -->
<p>Corvin looked at him.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p24 -->
<p>For the first time. Straight at him. Their faces a hand’s breadth apart. <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub>’s hand on his wrist, round it, gripping, with everything he had.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p25 · Corvin -->
<p>“Two,” said Corvin.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p26 · tension -->
<p><prosody rate="97%">He didn’t pull against <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub>’s hand. He didn’t try to shake it off. He knelt there with <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub> holding his wrist, and looked at him with his grey eyes, and <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub> pulled, and pulled, and the hand didn’t move off the key. It was like pulling at a tree.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p27 -->
<p>Not strength, <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub> thought. He’s not stronger than me. He’s a thin man with a clerk’s hands.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p28 -->
<p>He just won’t.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p29 · Calder (bond, to Kharrak) -->
<p><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB"><sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub>…</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p30 · urgent -->
<p><prosody rate="105%"><sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub> was in the chamber. Behind him. Rock still coming down. <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub> felt him coming, felt the heat on his back, felt the red tide going up and over, felt <sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub> see the key and the hand and the wrist…</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p31 · Corvin -->
<p>“One,” said Corvin.</p>
<break time="1600ms"/><!-- scene break -->
<!-- p32 -->
<p>He turned it.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p33 · tension -->
<p><prosody rate="97%">With <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub>’s hand on his wrist. With <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub> pulling back against him with all his weight. He turned the long black key in the iron boss, and it turned as if it wanted to, as if it had been waiting three hundred years to be turned and was glad.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p34 -->
<p>And the whole stone disc turned with it.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p35 · awe -->
<p><prosody rate="95%"><sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub> felt it go under his knees. The great carved floor as wide as a threshing floor, grinding, turning, a quarter of a turn. The rings of letters cut in it sliding past each other. Ring past ring. The letters in each ring meeting the letters in the next, and stopping, in a line. A line of letters from the rim to the iron boss, all at once, where there’d been no line before.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p36 -->
<p>It lit. The whole line, white, rim to boss, so bright it came up through his knees and he saw the bones of his own hand round Corvin’s wrist, dark inside the skin.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p37 -->
<p>The grinding stopped.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p38 -->
<p>And in the same breath, a long way off, under the river, toward Greyhold, the same sound.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p39 · awe -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">He felt it through his knees. Through the stone disc. Through the rock. Far off. So far off he couldn’t tell if it was a sound or only the ground. A great slow grinding turn. The same. In the same breath. As if somewhere a long way away, under the other bank, under the school, another floor had turned under another hand at the same moment as this one.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p40 · Calder (thought) -->
<p><prosody rate="97%" volume="-4dB">Two hands.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p41 -->
<p>Corvin felt it too. <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub> saw him feel it. Kneeling on the iron boss with his hand on the key and <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub>’s hand on his wrist, he lifted his head, very slightly, listening.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p42 -->
<p>And he smiled.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p43 · dread: a satisfied smile -->
<p><prosody rate="96%">It was the only time <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub> ever saw him do it. A small smile. Not like his brother’s. Satisfied. The smile of a man at the weighing-post when the sack comes out at the weight he said.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p44 -->
<p>Then he let go of the key, and <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub>’s hand came away with nothing in it, and Corvin was up and walking across the lit stone to the rim as if he’d paced it out beforehand. <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub>, held by the grinding in the stone, couldn’t get up off his knees to follow.</p>
<break time="1600ms"/><!-- scene break -->
<!-- p45 -->
<p>The seal opened.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p46 -->
<p>He’d thought it would be a door. Something that swung, or slid, or lifted.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p47 · action -->
<p><prosody rate="104%">The floor went. The stone disc dropped. All of it. Out from under him. Dropping, whole, like a trap-door, and he was on it, kneeling, and then there was nothing under his knees at all. And the chamber floor round it went too, the rock round the rim cracking away in a great ring and going down after it. The passage too, and the ledge beyond it. The grey man went down with the disc, lying where he’d fallen, and didn’t move.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p48 -->
<p>And above.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p49 · awe: the Ruin falling -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">He felt it above. Through the marks. The tower. The round room at its foot where <sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub> had dug through. The arch. The lion’s long smooth hollow in the threshold. The verse over the arch, six lines, <prosody rate="95%">let no hand wake it.</prosody> All of it, cracking, going down. The fort round it. The broken walls. The great fire in the middle of the fort, falling into the hole. The Old Ruin, that had stood on its island in the river since before there was a <sub alias="Harthmeer">Hearthmere</sub>, since there was a bridge, falling into the dark under it all at once with a sound like the end of the world.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p50 -->
<p>He fell.</p>
<break time="1600ms"/><!-- scene break -->
<!-- p51 -->
<p>He fell for a long time.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p52 · action -->
<p><prosody rate="104%">He didn’t know which way was up. Rock falling round him, past him, with him. Dust. Darkness, and in the darkness, now and then, fire, <sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub>’s, white, lighting the falling stone for a moment like a lantern swung in a mill. He heard <sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub> roar. Close. Then further. He felt <sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub>’s wings jam in the falling rock and tear free and jam again.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p53 -->
<p>He felt the ground of the cavern coming up at him out of the dark, a long way down. He couldn’t see it. He knew it was there. The way you know the bottom of a well is there when you drop a stone.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p54 · grief · Calder (thought) -->
<p><prosody rate="94%"><prosody rate="97%" volume="-4dB">I’m sorry,</prosody> he thought. <prosody rate="97%" volume="-4dB">Wren. I’m sorry.</prosody></prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p55 -->
<p>Something came down through the falling rock above him.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p56 · urgent -->
<p><prosody rate="105%">Fast. Faster than the rock. Wings folded, head down, like a stone thrown at the bottom of the world. Bronze. Huge. With one gold eye and the ruin where the other had been, and blood all down the plates of her chest where the ironback’s horn had been in her.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p57 -->
<p>He felt her come. Through the bronze mark. He felt her tear free of the ironback in the fort as the fort went in under her, and fold her wings, and dive into the hole after him.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p58 -->
<p>Her forefoot closed round him in the dark.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p59 · tender -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">Round his whole body, as his hand would close round an egg. Claws as long as his arm, curved over him like the bars of a cage. Holding.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p60 -->
<p>She couldn’t stop.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p61 -->
<p>She opened her wings.</p>
<break time="1600ms"/><!-- scene break -->
<!-- p62 -->
<p>He felt them open. He’d felt her wings open a thousand times, on the hill, in the sky over the Marches, over the river at midwinter. He’d never felt this.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p63 · awe -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">She opened her wings in the cavern under the Old Ruin, in the dark, among the falling stone, the first wings that had ever opened in that air in all the years since there’d been a cavern. They caught. The air was there. More air than he’d thought, more dark, more room. A great dark, going on and on in every direction past where any light could reach. They caught the air and she turned, and the falling stone went past them, and she was flying.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p64 -->
<p>Not well. Not long. She was hurt and heavy and the ironback’s horn had been in her chest. She came down in a long slanting rush through the dark with the rock still falling round them, and the sound of it going on above, and her wings beating once, twice, three times, and then the ground.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p65 · action -->
<p><prosody rate="104%">A slope. Rubble. She hit it hard on her hind legs and her chest and slid, and he felt her forefoot keep him off the stones, curled round him, while she slid down the rubble on her bronze plates with a noise like a ploughshare on rock. A long way. Then she stopped.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p66 -->
<p>She lay there.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p67 -->
<p>He lay in her forefoot.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p68 · quiet -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">The rock went on falling. Above them, behind them, out in the dark, the rest of the Old Ruin coming down. It went on and on. Then smaller. Then stones, one at a time, rattling down the slope. Then nothing.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p69 -->
<p>The dust settled.</p>
<break time="1600ms"/><!-- scene break -->
<!-- p70 · Aurveth (bond, to Calder) -->
<p><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB"><sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub>,</prosody> said <sub alias="Orveth">Aurveth</sub>.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p71 · Calder -->
<p>“Yes.”</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p72 · Aurveth (bond, to Calder) -->
<p><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">Are you…</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p73 · Calder -->
<p>“Yes.” He didn’t know if he was. He moved his arms. His legs. Everything hurt. Everything moved. “Yes. Are you?”</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p74 -->
<p>She didn’t answer.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p75 · grief -->
<p><prosody rate="94%">He felt her through the bronze mark and he didn’t need her to. The horn-wound in her chest, deep, pulsing. Her wings, the left one wrenched, the joint torn. Her back, the old scars from the mill opened again. She lay on the rubble with her great head down on the stones and her breath going in and out of her, slow, ragged, and he felt every bit of it.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p76 · Calder -->
<p>“<sub alias="Orveth">Aurveth</sub>.”</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p77 · tender: slow, old, hurt · Aurveth (bond, to Calder) -->
<p><prosody rate="95%"><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">I’m here,</prosody> she said. <prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">I’ve been here before.</prosody> A long pause. <prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">Not here. But hurt like this. I’m old. I’ve been hurt like this.</prosody></prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p78 -->
<p>Her forefoot opened.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p79 -->
<p>He crawled out of it onto the rubble.</p>
<break time="1600ms"/><!-- scene break -->
<!-- p80 -->
<p>It was dark. Somewhere above, very far up, there was light: a ragged hole, orange, where the island had been, with fire still burning at the edges of it, a long way up. It didn’t reach down here. It lit the dust hanging in the air above them, and the edges of things, and nothing else.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p81 -->
<p><sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub> came down the slope.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p82 -->
<p>Out of the dark above them. Sliding, clawing, falling and catching himself, in a shower of loose stone, with his wings half open and jammed with rubble and his head down. He came down the slope of fallen rock onto the stones beside them and stopped, and stood there, swaying.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p83 · quiet -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">Cut. Burned. One horn broken off short. Blood running down his side from the ironback and from the rock and from the digging, and his claws torn. Alive.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p84 -->
<p>He put his head down to <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub>.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p85 · Kharrak (bond, to Calder) -->
<p><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">You’re alive,</prosody> said <sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub>.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p86 · Calder -->
<p>“Yes.”</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p87 · Kharrak (bond, to Calder), low -->
<p><prosody rate="94%" volume="-6dB">I felt you fall.</prosody> The red tide was low. <prosody rate="94%" volume="-6dB">I couldn’t reach you. I was in the rock.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p88 · Calder -->
<p>“She caught me.”</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p89 -->
<p><sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub> looked at <sub alias="Orveth">Aurveth</sub>, lying on the stones.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p90 · tender -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">He lay down beside her, close, against her side, and put his head on her neck. She let him.</prosody></p>
<break time="1600ms"/><!-- scene break -->
<!-- p91 -->
<p>He heard the ironback go past.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p92 -->
<p>Out in the dark below them. Something huge coming down the slope of rubble from above, not sliding, falling, end over end, plates and horn and the great humped back, and past them, close enough that the wind of it went over his face, and on, down, into a deeper dark below the slope.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p93 · quiet -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">It didn’t make a sound when it hit.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p94 · quiet -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">The man in grey who’d stood on its neck with his arm up didn’t make one either.</prosody></p>
<break time="1600ms"/><!-- scene break -->
<!-- p95 -->
<p>He looked for Corvin.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p96 -->
<p>He couldn’t see much. The dust. The dark. The fire very far up. But across the cavern, on the far side of the great hole the Old Ruin had fallen into, high up on the wall of the dark, there was a light.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p97 -->
<p>A lantern. Small. Yellow. Moving.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p98 -->
<p>Going up.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p99 -->
<p>He watched it. It went up slowly, back and forth, back and forth. A stair he hadn’t known was there. An older one. Cut into the far wall of the cavern, going up to somewhere he couldn’t see. Three figures with it. One tall and thin, going first, not hurrying, not looking down.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p100 · anger -->
<p>Corvin had known it was there. Of course he had. He’d read the verse. He’d read the cut pages, or the ones that hadn’t been cut, or whatever the Restoration had that <sub alias="Harthmeer">Hearthmere</sub> didn’t. He’d known the floor would go. He’d knelt on the iron boss with his hand on the key and counted down to one and turned it, and when the floor went he’d already been at the edge of it, and the stair.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p101 -->
<p>The lantern went up the far wall and round a corner of the rock, and was gone.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p102 -->
<p>He didn’t look back once.</p>
<break time="1600ms"/><!-- scene break -->
<!-- p103 -->
<p><sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub> stood up on the rubble.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p104 -->
<p>He stood at the bottom of the slope of the fallen Ruin with the two dragons lying behind him, and looked out into the dark.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p105 -->
<p>There were the chains.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p106 · awe -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">He could see them now. His eyes had found them. Going up past him into the dark above, toward the hole and the fire, where they’d been fixed to whatever had been above. Six. Black. Each link taller than a man. Taut. So taut they hummed. A deep note, all six together, that went through the rock and through his boots and through his teeth.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p107 -->
<p>And going down. Ahead of him. Into a deeper dark at the bottom of the cavern, further than the slope, further than anything. Down to where they were fastened to whatever they’d been fastened to for three hundred years.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p108 -->
<p>Something was moving down there.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p109 · dread -->
<p><prosody rate="96%">Not the dark moving, or water turning over. Something he couldn’t see the edges of, that filled the deep dark at the bottom of the cavern, lifting, as a hill would lift if a hill could stand up.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p110 -->
<p>The chains groaned.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p111 -->
<p>Up at the top of the slope, where the six chains went up into the dark toward the hole, there were stones. Great anchor-stones, set in the cavern wall, each as big as a house, with the chains running through iron eyes in them. He could see the nearest one in the light of the fire far above.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p112 -->
<p>It was cracking.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p113 · dread -->
<p><prosody rate="96%">A long dark line running across the face of it, from the iron eye outward. Getting longer as he watched, like ice on a pond in the morning when somebody’s walking out on it.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p114 · Calder (thought) -->
<p><prosody rate="97%" volume="-4dB">Two hands,</prosody> he thought. <prosody rate="97%" volume="-4dB">Here and there. And it wakes.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p115 · dread · Calder (thought) -->
<p><prosody rate="96%"><prosody rate="97%" volume="-4dB">And it will not sleep again.</prosody></prosody></p>
<break time="1600ms"/><!-- scene break -->
<!-- p116 -->
<p>He felt something.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p117 -->
<p>Far off. Not from the hole where the Ruin had been, where the fire was. The other way. Across the cavern, through the rock, toward the far side of the river. Toward the <sub alias="Harthmeer">Hearthmere</sub> bank. Toward Greyhold.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p118 · quiet -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">A small bright fire. Green. Frightened. Far off, under the other bank, and still.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p119 -->
<p>He stood on the rubble and stared into the dark toward it.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p120 · Calder (bond, to Lisska) -->
<p><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB"><sub alias="Liska">Lisska</sub>?</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p121 -->
<p>No answer. No words. Too far still, through too much rock. But the feeling. He’d know it anywhere. He’d felt it go west over the Brackenwood at first light with a bundle in her claw, going further and further until it was nearly nothing.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p122 -->
<p>Now it was there again. On the far side of the river, by the school. Still.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p123 -->
<p>He didn’t understand it.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p124 · Calder (thought) -->
<p><prosody rate="97%" volume="-4dB">How?</prosody> he thought. <prosody rate="97%" volume="-4dB">What’s she doing at the school?</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p125 -->
<p>Beside it, so close to it he could hardly tell them apart, there was something else.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p126 · awe -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">Not his. He couldn’t feel it the way he felt her. He felt it through her, the way he’d felt Morrow through <sub alias="Orveth">Aurveth</sub> at the ford. Something very large, and very old, and warm, like the ground in summer. Somewhere under her, down in the dark.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p127 -->
<p>With it, smaller, almost nothing, so faint he’d have missed it if <sub alias="Liska">Lisska</sub> hadn’t been holding on to it the way she held on to him: somebody.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p128 · quiet -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">A person.</prosody></p>
<break time="1800ms"/>
</speak>
